{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Systems\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"Schedule","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L100"},"externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering"],"title":"Creating a Schedule","anchor":"Creating-a-Schedule"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runSerially(on:)"],"title":"Running Systems","anchor":"Running-Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/after(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/before(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/inSet(_:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguous(with:)","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/runIf(_:)"],"title":"Ordering and Conditioning Every System","anchor":"Ordering-and-Conditioning-Every-System"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/writeDOT(to:)"],"title":"Inspecting a Schedule","anchor":"Inspecting-a-Schedule"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A schedule holds the systems of one frame or step of a simulation. You build it by listing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the systems in a closure, and run it on a world with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs each system once:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 2, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 70.0)\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Ordering-Systems","level":3,"text":"Ordering Systems","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order they’re written, except where an ordering constraint requires","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. A system that must run after one written later, by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"text":", or before one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written earlier, by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"text":", is moved to satisfy the constraint, and every other system","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its written place:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let frame = Schedule {","    Scoring().after(Movement.self)","    Movement()","    Gravity().before(Movement.self)","}","print(frame.names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gravity\", \"Movement\", \"Scoring\"]\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A constraint naming a type with no system in the schedule is ignored, and one naming a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s own type doesn’t order the system against itself. Constraints that form a cycle,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so that no order satisfies them all, trap; build the schedule with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/init(checked:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to throw","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Running-Systems-at-the-Same-Time","level":3,"text":"Running Systems at the Same Time","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"conflict"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when one writes a type the other reads or writes, or when either has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" runs conflicting systems in order and the rest at the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time. The world ends as though the systems had run one after another in order, except that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the commands systems queue apply when their wave finishes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, the order they run in rests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only on how they happen to be written. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"text":" lists those pairs, so a test can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguous(with:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"ambiguous(with:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguous(with:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns this schedule with each of its systems free to run in either order with every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system in each of the given sets."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguous(with:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguous","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/names":{"title":"names","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"names"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/names","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The names of the schedule’s systems’ types, in the order the systems run."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/names","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/systems":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/systems","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The schedule’s systems, in the order they run."}],"title":"systems","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"systems","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems15ScheduledSystemV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentat